,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-07-27T04:16:19Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T15:25:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121814","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121814","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121814.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121814.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nWhen `exp_edit` is enabled on a `Range` node and `min_value` is set to `0`, setting `ratio` to `0` currently yields a `value` of `1`. Moreover, if `min_value` is `0` and `max_value` is less than `1`, the slider becomes completely unusable.\r\n\r\nThis happens because the internal mapping treats `0` as `1` to avoid undefined behaviour of `log(0)`, which brings the inconsistency. The solution is to shift the range with a small positive epsilon before taking the logarithm when `min_value` is zero, and then shift the value back. The chosen epsilon (`1e-3`) is the same as the default step of `EditorSpinSlider`, which avoids a steep curve and unintended non‑zero values displayed as zero.\r\n\r\n- Closes #121804\r\n- Closes #109248\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis PR also removes a redundant calculation in `ProgressBar`, and the fix only affects `Range` and its child classes, specifically when `min_value` is exactly `0`.\r\n\r\nThis PR implements one of the approaches discussed in #121804.\r\n\r\nTests were done on MRPs from #121804 and #109248, and worked as expected.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121814/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121814/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}